# Manual testing checklist

Run these checks after installing dependencies and before pushing changes.

## Startup and dataset

- [ ] `python app.py` starts without an import error.
- [ ] The homepage loads at `http://127.0.0.1:5000/`.
- [ ] A missing `responses.csv` produces a clear message rather than an unhandled traceback.
- [ ] A valid dataset loads and the page reports the number of usable profiles.
- [ ] Missing optional columns do not silently turn personal/contact fields into model features.

## Existing profile flow

- [ ] The user selector lists available profiles.
- [ ] Submitting without a selected profile gives a helpful message.
- [ ] Recommendations do not include the selected profile itself.
- [ ] Same-cluster and outside-cluster results are displayed in the appropriate sections.
- [ ] The same-gender filter behaves as documented.
- [ ] Empty or very small candidate groups are handled gracefully.

## Manual profile flow

- [ ] A new profile can be submitted with valid values.
- [ ] Empty names and invalid numeric values produce helpful validation messages.
- [ ] Values outside the intended range are rejected or normalized consistently.
- [ ] Submitting an existing name has the expected update behaviour.
- [ ] Saving a profile does not damage the original CSV columns or rows.
- [ ] The new profile is not recommended as its own match.

## Privacy and deployment

- [ ] No real student data is committed.
- [ ] Debug mode is disabled before deployment.
- [ ] Errors shown to users do not reveal file paths or sensitive information.
- [ ] The dataset write path and access permissions are appropriate for the environment.
